'''Larry Thomas Pridemore Jr.''' (born April 29, 1956) is a former [[Safety (football position)|safety]] from West Virginia who played eight seasons in the [[National Football League]] (NFL) for the [[Atlanta Falcons]] and served as a delegate in the [[West Virginia House of Delegates]] from 1981–1983.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.s9.com/Biography/Tom-Pridemore|title=Tom Pridemore - Biographical Dictionary - s9.com|date=8 August 2015|publisher=}}</ref>
